*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local development framework.
# Two things are tracked here: the STATE RECORD (state.json plus its four
# rendered views, Loop 4 C4) and the INSTRUCTION SURFACE — every file that
# tells an agent what to do in a session (Loop 11, session 62).
#
# Until 2026-09-17 the instruction surface was ignored entirely: 39 of 77
# instruction files were absent from history, CLAUDE.md among them, so a
# fresh clone got no instructions at all and a repair to a live command
# appeared in no diff and could not be restored. Only project-template/ —
# the copy shipped to other projects — was versioned.
#
# Still local by intent: session logs, archive/, working task specs,
# .claude/settings.local.json, and third-party plugin skills.
/.agents/*
!/.agents/state.json
!/.agents/AGENT.md
!/.agents/LIFECYCLE.md
!/.agents/retirements.json
!/.agents/TASKS/
/.agents/TASKS/*
!/.agents/TASKS/INBOX.md
!/.agents/TASKS/task.md
!/.agents/SESSIONS/
/.agents/SESSIONS/*
!/.agents/SESSIONS/next-session.md
!/.agents/SYSTEM/
/.agents/SYSTEM/*
!/.agents/SYSTEM/SUMMARY.md
!/.agents/SYSTEM/RULES.md
!/.agents/SYSTEM/RUNBOOK.md
!/.agents/SYSTEM/SECURITY.md
!/.agents/SYSTEM/TESTING.md
!/.agents/SYSTEM/domains.json
!/.agents/SYSTEM/worktree-seats.json
# PRD/DECISIONS/ENTITIES: THE SCOPE LAYER TRAVELS. Tracked 2026-09-21 (session 77) after a
# planner seat spent a whole session without knowing what the project is for. Everything
# tracked above is HOW TO OPERATE; these three are WHAT THIS IS AND WHY, and they were the
# only ones left out. An untracked file reaches ONE checkout: PRD.md existed in the main tree
# and in none of the three seat worktrees, where every seat actually works. /sync had been
# reporting `PRD.md not found` as a WARNING on every run in those trees and it was read past
# every time. This is the roles/ lesson below, which says it was relearned 2026-09-19 --
# two lines away from the rule that was still hiding the PRD.
!/.agents/SYSTEM/PRD.md
!/.agents/SYSTEM/DECISIONS.md
!/.agents/SYSTEM/ENTITIES.md
!/.agents/skills/
/.agents/skills/*
!/.agents/skills/INDEX.md
!/.agents/skills/self-improving-agent-gotchas/
!/.agents/skills/self-improving-agent-guide/
# roles/: SEAT KNOWLEDGE IS TRACKED; only the seat's NAME is local. AGENT.local.md is
# gitignored by design (a per-checkout override must not be versioned), and role guidance
# written into it would exist on one disk, in one ignored file, invisible to a fresh clone
# and destroyed by moving the worktree. Same lesson as the block above, relearned 2026-09-19.
!/.agents/roles/
/.agents/roles/*
!/.agents/roles/*.md
# .claude/: the live commands are tracked; local settings and plugin skills are not.
/.claude/*
!/.claude/commands/
# docs/: working material stays local, but LOOP CLOSE-OUTS ARE THE RECORD and are tracked.
# Loop 10's six docs were tracked only because someone remembered `git add -f`; Loop 11's
# close-out was silently dropped from its own commit because nobody did. A rule that must be
# remembered is not a rule (Loop 10 R4), so the negation replaces the habit.
# The parent must be `/docs/*` rather than `/docs/` — git cannot re-include a file whose
# parent DIRECTORY is excluded.
/docs/*
!/docs/loops/
# HOH-JEV.md is the LOOP GUIDE — the standing contract for how a loop runs, which seat may
# write what, and how the Jev gates are called. It began as an untracked file in one
# worktree and was being used as the guide from there, which is the same defect as the
# close-outs above: a source of truth on one disk, invisible to a fresh clone.
!/docs/HOH-JEV.md

# Runtime artifacts (session-local / regenerated)
/.recalled-entries.json
/open-brain/.agents/
AGENTS.md

# WIP — not ready for public repo yet
/a2a-wrapper/
.gitnexus

# Build artifacts
open-brain/build/

# hoh_jev.md is the ORIGINAL BRIEF Aaron wrote for the HoH + Jev loop, tracked 2026-09-20 on his
# word. docs/HOH-JEV.md is the binding guide and names where it diverges from this file (its
# section 6); this file is kept so the divergences can be checked against their source.
!/docs/hoh_jev.md
